# L1 Interface Testnet — operator overrides (TEMPLATE)
#
# Copy this file to `l1-interface.local.env` and fill in the values that depend
# on YOUR infrastructure:
#
#   cp envs/testnet/l1-interface.local.env.example envs/testnet/l1-interface.local.env
#
# The real `l1-interface.local.env` is gitignored (it holds endpoints/credentials)
# and is loaded AFTER the generated `l1-interface.env`, so anything set here wins.
# Keep secrets (RPC API keys, passwords) out of version control.

# --- Optional: override the bundled public Ethereum Sepolia execution RPC ---
# The generated testnet configuration defaults to:
#   https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com
# Uncomment this only when using your own provider. The endpoint and plan must
# allow chain ID 11155111 and standard execution methods including
# eth_getBlockByHash. Keep any endpoint API key in this gitignored file.
# Recreate l1-interface after changing this value; a plain `docker compose
# restart` does not reload environment files.
# DOGEOS_L1_INTERFACE_ETHEREUM_DA__L1_RPC_URL=https://your-ethereum-l1-rpc:8545

# --- Optional: only for a generated config that selects beacon_node DA ---
# The tracked testnet package uses the public AWS S3 blob source instead.
# DOGEOS_L1_INTERFACE_ETHEREUM_DA__BLOB_SOURCE__BEACON_NODE__URL=http://your-beacon:5052

# --- Optional: temporary/debug external Dogecoin RPC override ---
# The RPC package defaults to the user's own Compose dogecoin-node, and its
# credentials come from DOGECOIN_RPC_USER and DOGECOIN_RPC_PASSWORD in the
# local Compose env file. Set these only for temporary/debug use.
# DOGEOS_L1_INTERFACE_DOGECOIN_RPC__URL=https://your-dogecoin-rpc
# DOGEOS_L1_INTERFACE_DOGECOIN_RPC__USER=your-provider-user
# DOGEOS_L1_INTERFACE_DOGECOIN_RPC__PASS=your-provider-password
